  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>40</x>
      <y>1140</y>
      <w>560</w>
      <h>160</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>One user, two access mechanisms
Swing GUI and CLI use the same system.
Local CSV, tools and validation are internal.
F04 checks are deterministic; listing
interpretation and clarification are separate.
F07 does not match vehicle body type.
fontsize=20
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>640</x>
      <y>1140</y>
      <w>560</w>
      <h>160</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Explicit user control
F02: review/correct, then confirm saving.
F11: answer/resolve/skip/unknown;
continue risk or checklist only on request.
F09: saved A and independent saved B.
No automatic use-case chaining is implied.
fontsize=20
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1240</x>
      <y>1140</y>
      <w>560</w>
      <h>160</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Evidence and fallback
Model participation is conditional.
F10 can return a deterministic fallback.
F12 reuses only current risk when available;
it does not automatically request F08.
Buyer TXT export is part of F12.
fontsize=20
bg=white</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
</diagram>